# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: probe-ps1-done-check-misreads-utf16-report — Windows probe scripts flag complete runs INCOMPLETE
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-probe-ps1-done-check
#+DATE: 2026-10-08

* Symptom

Every Windows run of intersectwith-probe (jobs 17029587294, 17029587295,
17029587296, 2026-10-08) ended its report with

: IWPROBE-INCOMPLETE  the probe did not reach its end

right after the =IWPROBE-DONE= line it claims is missing.

* Cause

The scripts write the report header with =Set-Content -Encoding utf8=
(UTF-8 BOM), then append with =Tee-Object -FilePath -Append=, which in
Windows PowerShell 5 writes UTF-16LE. The file is mixed (UTF-8 BOM + CRLF,
then UTF-16LE without BOM), and =Select-String -Path $report -Pattern
'^...-DONE'= reads it as UTF-8 and never matches.

* Resolution so far

run-intersectwith-probe.ps1 (clautolisp 2.3.10) decides on the captured
lines instead of re-reading the file. The same check is still in
run-getcname-probe.ps1, run-optkw-probe.ps1, run-path-sysvars-probe.ps1 and
run-pgp-probe.ps1 (=grep -l "Select-String -Path" scripts/*.ps1=).

* Proposal

Apply the same change to those four; better, write the report in ONE
encoding (=Out-File -Encoding utf8 -Append=, or collect and Set-Content
once), so the artefacts no longer need byte-level decoding.
